---
import ContactCTA from '../components/ContactCTA.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Blog | Side Quests Colorado" description="The monthly Side Quests Colorado events blog.">
	<div class="stack gap-20">
		<main class="wrapper about">
			<Hero
				title="Events Blog"
				tagline="The monthly Side Quests Colorado events blog."
			>
				<img
					width="1553"
					height="873"
					src="/assets/events.jpg"
					alt="Two women working together in garden to harvest."
				/>
			</Hero>
			<section>
				<h2 class="section-title">Blog Posts</h2>
				<div class="content">
				<p>Remember to check each group or events particpation criteria or RSVP method before going. Some groups are only open to individuals who identify a certain way. Some require RSVPs. Respect their participation rules.</p>
				<ul>
          			<li><a href="../posts/November26-Bikes/" target=_blank>November Bike Events</a></li>
					<li><a href="../posts/November26-BookClubs/" target=_blank>November Book Clubs</a></li>
					<li><a href="../posts/November26-Walking/" target=_blank>November Walking Events</a></li>
					<li><a href="../posts/November26-Writing/" target=_blank>November Writing Events</a></li>
					<li><a href="../posts/November26-Yoga/" target=_blank>November Yoga Classes</a></li>
					<li><a href="../posts/November26-OtherEvents/" target=_blank>More November Events</a></li>
					<li><a href="../posts/October26" target=_blank>October 2026</a></li>
        		</ul>
				</div>
			</section>
			<section>
				<h2 class="section-title">Respect</h2>
				<div class="content">
					<p class="space-p">Not all the events posted are open to everyone. Some events are for specific groups (like the LGBTQIA+ community or BIPOC individuals). We may accidentally also publish events open for members of a club/organization as well (though we'll try not to). Please respect each event and/or each organization or groups participation criteria. Remember that people are often going to these events looking for genuine human connection, and sometimes that is easier when you can find and exist with people like you. Sometimes people want to find this by seeking out people who are different from them. Both are okay. Respect everyone's right to get-together with whom they choose and don't crash an event intended for an identity that isn't yours.</p>
					<p>We probably didn't write that very well but we hope you 1) understand we don't want to cause any organization or individual a problem by sending folks to their event who were not invited and 2) that we want everyone looking for events to have a good time. Thank you for understanding. </p>
					</div>
				<h2 class="section-title">Disclaimer</h2>
				<div class="content">
					<p>
						These events are not hosted by or affiliated with Colorado Side Quests in any way shape or form. Colorado Side Quests does not endorse any group or organization tied to these events. You must do your own research about any event or organization you intend to participate in. You are responsible for your own safety both in-person and online. **Use any of the content on Colorado Side Quests at your own risk.**
					</p>
					</div>
			</section>
			
		</main>
		

		<ContactCTA />
	</div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.space-p{
		padding-bottom: 1rem;
	}
	.about {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 3.5rem;
	}

	img {
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
		border-radius: 1.5rem;
		box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
	}

	section {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		color: var(--gray-200);
	}

	.section-title {
		grid-column-start: 1;
		font-size: var(--text-xl);
		color: var(--gray-0);
	}

	.content {
		grid-column: 2 / 4;
	}

	.content :global(a) {
		text-decoration: 1px solid underline transparent;
		text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
		transition: text-decoration-color var(--theme-transition);
	}

	.content :global(a:hover),
	.content :global(a:focus) {
		text-decoration-color: currentColor;
	}

	@media (min-width: 50em) {
		.about {
			display: grid;
			grid-template-columns: 1fr 60% 1fr;
		}

		.about > :global(:first-child) {
			grid-column-start: 2;
		}

		section {
			display: contents;
			font-size: var(--text-lg);
		}
	}
</style>
